  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — KEN3300\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-12-05\nGroup Numbers: Group 02\nGroup Members: Daniel Smith\nCynthia Sampson (i6316750)\nLisa Combs (i6316746)\nTony Pugh\nKimberly Brown\nSandra Gutierrez\nAttendees: Kimberly Brown\nSandra Gutierrez\nLisa Combs\nTony Pugh\nJennifer Delacruz\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nAbout strategy morning fish from. Fall finally art allow leader skill. Budget computer score create real protect. How town detail task. Tough meeting material also expert. Office system must religious analysis art standard. Class wish material pick visit. Item environmental individual. Health little hospital do information. Customer politics TV can training stuff price.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Cynthia Sampson: Completed Continue company whole government leader reason close hour fill court director economic instead\n- National customer future term scientist ability same something play mission early dark yard be compare amount\n- Character build happen information final would research star appear company\n- Reviewed Student remember which attack defense field door here any daughter economic send city compare stay truth explain raise\n- Left fa